# Vercel serves the pre-built dist/ directory as a static site (see
# vercel.json) -- the pipeline itself runs in GitHub Actions
# (.github/workflows/refresh.yml), never on Vercel. Excluding every .py
# file here isn't just cleanup: Vercel's zero-config "Other" framework
# preset auto-detects any top-level .py file as a Python serverless
# function entrypoint (expecting an "app"/"application"/"handler"
# variable) independently of vercel.json's buildCommand -- main.py is a
# CLI script, not a web handler, which is exactly the "does not export a
# top-level app/application/handler" build error this avoids.
main.py
src/
dashboard/build_dashboard.py
requirements.txt
data/
.github/
.env.example
